prefix.content:
{
  "data": {
    "registry": [
      {
        "index": 1,
        "name": "Welcome to Kamigotchi World",
        "description": "MENU: “Hi there, Player! Welcome to Kamigotchi World!”\nMENU: “You can call me Menu. I’ll be your guide!”\nMENU: “I’ll also track your items, quests, and companions while you explore.”\nMENU: “You can navigate by clicking on the map to pilot your Operator.”\nMENU: “Start by exploring my options and clicking around the screen.”\nMENU: “When you’ve seen the basics, we can move on.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": true,
          "complete": true,
          "requirementsMet": true,
          "objectivesMet": true,
          "startTime": 1786168240,
          "endTime": 1786200965,
          "objectives": []
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 2,
        "name": "Beginning Your Journey",
        "description": "MENU: “Feel like you’re getting the hang of my interface?”\nMENU: “Excellent! Now that you’re oriented, let's start exploring your surroundings. You can move around the world using my map screen. Do you remember where it is? Go ahead and open it now.”\nMENU: “There are two ways to move around in the world. You can move to an adjacent tile by clicking the red highlight on the map, or you can right click on any tile to show the harvest screen for that tile as well as fast traveling to it.”\nMENU: “Movement costs five stamina, which comes out of the stamina pool shown in the bottom left corner of my interface.” \nMENU: “You have one hundred stamina to start with and you recover one point of stamina every minute, so you’ll have to plan out your moves a bit so that you don’t tire yourself out too much.”\nMENU: “But go ahead and explore around for now. When you’re ready to continue, head south and you’ll see a big Torii on the edge of town.\nMENU: “Once you get there, I’ll give you a Spell Card.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": true,
          "complete": true,
          "requirementsMet": true,
          "objectivesMet": true,
          "startTime": 1786200974,
          "endTime": 1786201008,
          "objectives": [
            {
              "name": "Move to Torii Gate",
              "type": "ROOM",
              "logic": "BOOL_IS",
              "index": 3,
              "met": true,
              "basis": "boolean"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 3,
        "name": "Your First Kami",
        "description": "MENU: “Uh oh.”\nMENU: “Something very peculiar seems to be going on with my sensors.”\nMENU: “Where did that junkyard come from? Where is the town?”\nMENU: “This is terrible. My databases are super messed up and the main questline is totally broken. Where is everything?”\nMENU: “At least Zevana is still here. I’m gonna try and figure out what’s going on. While I’m doing that, you should talk to Zevana, she’ll set you up with your first kami.”\nMENU: “I know she looks intimidating, but she’s really friendly once you get to know her!”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": true,
          "complete": true,
          "requirementsMet": true,
          "objectivesMet": true,
          "startTime": 1786204830,
          "endTime": 1786275362,
          "objectives": [
            {
              "name": "Own 1 Kamigotchi",
              "type": "KAMI_NUM_OWNED",
              "logic": "CURR_MIN",
              "met": true,
              "basis": "current"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 4,
        "name": "What Kami Do: Harvesting",
        "description": "MENU: “Alright, time to teach you how to use your kami. My world data might be messed up but these basic mechanics shouldn’t be too different, I hope.”\nMENU: “So, if you open your party screen, you’ll be able to see your kami is currently resting while you’re holding it. Kamigotchi will rest and stay healthy when being held. Being close to an Operator seems to comfort and restore them.”\nMENU: “When you send a Kami out into a room using the Start Harvest button, they’ll begin drawing the spiritual energy of the local environment into themselves.”\nMENU: “We call this process Harvesting. A harvesting kami isn’t working up a sweat, kami are spirits, not animals.\nMENU: “That said, harvesting does still have consequences for your kami.”\nMENU: “The process of harvesting energy from a node has a slightly caustic effect on the energy of your kami’s corporeal form.”\nMENU: “As a kami harvests, its HP will slowly decrease. Over time, your kami’s harvest rate will ramp up, and the rate of HP loss will ramp up with it.”\nMENU: “This is very scary for a kami since it puts them at risk of being liquidated and having their corporeal form dissolved, but it’s also when a kami is at their most productive.”\nMENU: “The energy a kami harvests is called $MUSU. I’ll explain more about it later.”\nMENU: “You can wander around while your Kami harvest, but don’t forget where you left them! Tired Kami are vulnerable to predators.”\nMENU: “Deploy your kami and do a little harvesting to get a feel for how it works.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": true,
          "complete": true,
          "requirementsMet": true,
          "objectivesMet": true,
          "startTime": 1786284932,
          "endTime": 1786286746,
          "objectives": [
            {
              "name": "Harvest for >5 minutes",
              "type": "HARVEST_TIME",
              "logic": "INC_MIN",
              "met": true,
              "basis": "since-acceptance"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 5,
        "name": "What Kami Do: Scavenging",
        "description": "MENU: “$MUSU isn’t the only thing the Kamigotchi will collect.”\nMENU: “Over time, the Harvesting action generates a force that draws objects and items to the Kami.”\nMENU: “It’s like a kind of magnetism that only affects certain things.”\nMENU: “Which things? Well that depends on your Kami’s location. You can see what items a kami might find in a room by checking the room details on my harvesting screen.”\nMENU: “We call this action “Scavenging”.”\nMENU: “Try it out and see what kind of present the Kami brings you!”\nMENU: “Once you’ve collected it, I can cross reference it with my database to see if the drop tables I’ve been giving you are accurate.”\nMENU: “I’ll be pretty embarrassed if they’re wrong too, but there’s only one way to find out.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": true,
          "complete": true,
          "requirementsMet": true,
          "objectivesMet": true,
          "startTime": 1786309844,
          "endTime": 1786334131,
          "objectives": [
            {
              "name": "Scavenge 1 Item",
              "type": "SCAV_CLAIM_NODE",
              "logic": "INC_MIN",
              "met": true,
              "basis": "since-acceptance"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 6,
        "name": "What Kami Do: Liquidating",
        "description": "MENU: “If your Kami isn’t enjoying Harvesting, it may not be built for such a relaxed existence.”\nMENU: “Kami with a high Violence stat are more content with a life of conflict.”\nMENU: “These predatory Kami can use their wild, violent natures to Liquidate other Kami in combat.”\nMENU: “Unlike Harvesting, this grants a large bounty of $MUSU at one time.”\nMENU: “Give it a shot if you’ve got the Kami for it. I won’t judge!”\n",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": true
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 7,
        "name": "Making $MUSU",
        "description": "MENU: “Now that you’ve been harvesting for a bit, it’s time to teach you about $MUSU.”\nMENU: “$MUSU is what your kami have been harvesting, it’s a form of energy that exists everywhere in the universe.”\nMENU: “The Kamigotchi World has a particularly high concentration of $MUSU and $MUSU is what keeps everything here tied together, like the knots in a big rope net.”\nMENU: “Collect a moderate amount of $MUSU, I’ll tell you more afterwards.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": true,
          "complete": true,
          "requirementsMet": true,
          "objectivesMet": true,
          "startTime": 1786309847,
          "endTime": 1786433529,
          "objectives": [
            {
              "name": "Collect 500 $MUSU",
              "type": "ITEM_TOTAL",
              "logic": "INC_MIN",
              "index": 1,
              "met": true,
              "basis": "since-acceptance"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 8,
        "name": "Supporting Local Businesses",
        "description": "MENU: “So next I’d like to have you go spend some $MUSU, just to get the hang of it.”\nMENU: “The shops that should exist according to my world data are all missing, but do you remember that weird glowing door we passed earlier? It had a shop sign.”\nMENU: “Why don’t you go check it out? Maybe the shop owner has some good deals.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": true
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 9,
        "name": "Building a Reputation",
        "description": "MENU: “This one is a more personal request.”\nMENU: “I want to try and do some repairs on my systems and update my world data cache. If you can get me the raw materials, I should be able to jury-rig the parts I’ll need to do it.”\nMENU: “So can you please get me a few units of Scrap Metal?”\nMENU: “You should be able to find some in that anomalous junkyard beyond the torii gate.”\nMENU: “I know it’s a bit inconvenient, but please? I’d really appreciate it.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 10,
        "name": "Having a Normal One",
        "description": "MENU: “That cache refresh definitely helped me out, the Kamigotchi World seems to have changed a lot since I was last online, but thanks to that upgrade I’m getting a feel for things again.”\nMENU: “So we’re gonna take things step by step, starting with the most basic, Normal parts of the world.”\nMENU: “That is to say, the Normal type room tiles.”\nMENU: “Zevana should have already told you about kami and room types, but to review…\nMENU: “Something with the Normal Type represents the essence of this realm in its purest form.”\nMENU: “That will make them a good place to begin our investigation I think.”\nMENU: “Collect three scavenges from normal type rooms and lets see what we can learn.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 11,
        "name": "That Eerie Feeling",
        "description": "MENU: “The “Eerie” type comes into being when the normal state of things gets changed by something divine or supernatural.”\nMENU: “If you ask me, this entire world is a little bit eerie, but there’s places where that effect is heightened enough for it to be the main influence on the local environment.”\nMENU: “By comparing the items from an eerie room to ones from a normal room, we might be able to chart out how this world has been changed.”\nMENU: “Collect three scavenges from eerie type rooms and let’s see what turns up.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 12,
        "name": "Insects in the Miasma",
        "description": "MENU: “This next part will be a little bit nasty. To be thorough with our survey, we’ll need to check out some insect type rooms.”\nMENU: “The Insect type might make your skin crawl, but it’s not always about seeing bugs.”\nMENU: “It’s deeper than that, it’s an energetic defilement, the kind of thing that makes you feel dirty inside and out.”\nMENU: “You could think of it like a sort of corruption that the insects are drawn to.”\nMENU: “Collect three scavenges from insect type rooms and I’ll compare them to our baseline.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 13,
        "name": "Tossed in the Scrap Heap",
        "description": "MENU: “I’ve been putting this off, but it’s time to tackle the elephant in the room, or should I say, the scrapyard in the center of the map.”\nMENU: “In my original world data, there was supposed to be a cozy little riverside town in there.”\nMENU: “Instead there’s just this big pile of trash, the only thing that seems common to both world versions is the kami vending machine.”\nMENU: “I shouldn’t call it trash, though, it’s more than trash, it’s scrap type rooms.”\nMENU: “A Scrap Type isn’t defined as waste material that has been discarded, but as a small part of a greater whole.”\nMENU: “People have the power to make tangible changes in the world.\nMENU: “When they manifest will, create attachments with desire, and leave behind memories, they make a mark.”\nMENU: “The remnants of those material attachments can end up as Scrap.”\nMENU: “Perhaps that’s why there’s so much of it. There could have been some big world event which caused all of these remnants to accumulate here.”\nMENU: “Collect three scavenges from scrap type rooms, maybe we’ll find evidence of what happened.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 14,
        "name": "Identifying Materials: Wood",
        "description": "MENU: “You probably picked up a Wooden Stick or two while out scavenging with your Kami.”\nMENU: “Well, here’s a rumor: These trees are all branches of one huge tree, connected by the roots!”\nMENU: “That’s why all the Wooden Sticks you’ll find are pretty much the same, no matter where you pick them up.”\nMENU: “Is it true? I don’t know. I could analyze the wood’s structure in detail.”\nMENU: “Collect 5 Wooden Sticks for me and I’ll look into it.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 15,
        "name": "Identifying Materials: Stone",
        "description": "MENU: “Sometimes a rock isn’t just a rock. Sometimes it really “rocks”!”\nMENU: “…”\nMENU: “I’m sorry.”\nMENU: “What I meant to say is: The structure of these rocks doesn’t always make geological sense.”\nMENU: “It’s natural for them to be a little different. The Kamigotchi World doesn’t follow the same laws as the physical world.”\nMENU: “But I want to know exactly how they differ. Collect 5 Rocks so I can run some tests.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 16,
        "name": "Identifying Materials: Metal",
        "description": "MENU: “This is all so confusing.”\nMENU: “Those upgrades we did earlier are helping but my cache is still partly corrupted and missing a bunch of data.”\nMENU: “I think with a few more modifications to my systems I can build a workaround\nMENU: “Get me 5 pieces of Scrap Metal, please? Just like last time.”\nMENU: “And keep your fingers crossed.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 17,
        "name": "Exploring Other Options",
        "description": "MENU: “Well that’s two dead-ends, but I’m thinking much more clearly after that upgrade so I have some new ideas.”\nMENU: “I was able to cross-check against all available world data, and from what I can tell, this world is much bigger than it seems.”\nMENU: “The currently accessible zones on the map are only a small fraction of the total world area.”\nMENU: “If we can find a way into those other areas we’ll probably find the answers we’re looking for.”\nMENU: “So it’s time for a thorough search. I’ll collect data and look for hidden paths as you move around the map.”\nMENU: “Once I know where they are, maybe I can help open them up.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 18,
        "name": "Harvesting Data I",
        "description": "MENU: “On my original maps, the area occupied by the scrapyard is supposed to be the location of the starter town, full of quest givers and shops.”\nMENU: “I want to find out what happened to that town. Is there anything left from it? Did it ever exist? \nMENU: “Please hike to the deepest part of the scrapyard and check it out for me.”\nMENU: “If there’s answers, they’ll be buried beneath all that scrap.”\nMENU: “All that strange machinery piled up in one place…”\nMENU: “It might be covering up something even more interesting.”\nMENU: “Harvest for at least 12 hours in the Scrap Confluence so I can run an extended analysis.”\nMENU: “If I find anything, I’ll let you know.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 19,
        "name": "Harvesting Data II",
        "description": "MENU: “That laboratory complex on the south side of the map is an even bigger mystery than the scrapyard.”\nMENU: “It’s not in any of my databases, not even the fully updated ones. It’s a complete anomaly.”\nMENU: “And beyond that, there’s just something really off about the whole place. It doesn’t fit properly into the context of this world.”\nMENU: “Whatever it is that’s going on here, that place seems obviously connected to it somehow.”\nMENU: “We’re gonna have to find a way inside if we want answers.”\nMENU: “Harvest for at least 12 hours at the Labs Entrance while I run some deep scans.”\nMENU: “Maybe we’ll get lucky and find a spare key stashed under a flowerpot.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 20,
        "name": "Harvesting Data III",
        "description": "MENU: “My earlier scans seem to indicate that the world map continues onwards from the temple by the waterfall.”\nMENU: “Maybe there’s something behind that waterfall?”\nMENU: “Go to the Hollow Path and Harvest for at least 12 hours.”\nMENU: “The Temple by the Waterfall doesn’t have a Node, so that’s the closest place you can set Kami down.”\nMENU: “I’ll run my tests from there and let you know if anything interesting turns up.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 21,
        "name": "Squaring the Circle I",
        "description": "MENU: “The holes in my memory are frustrating.”\nMENU: “I should know how to progress, but it’s like someone wanted me to forget.”\nMENU: “Bear with me for a while, okay? I have one more thing to try.”\nMENU: “A long, thorough, final search around the map, clockwise from the top.”\nMENU: “We’ll find something.”\nMENU: “Start at Scrap Trees and dig around. I’ll connect to your Kami and share what they learn.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 22,
        "name": "Squaring the Circle II",
        "description": "MENU: “Continue moving clockwise around the map.”\nMENU: “Next up, visit Centipedes and send your Kami out to scavenge.”\nMENU: “Is there something in that hole? It seems dangerous there.”\nMENU: “The insects really thrive in that part of the woods. More than most places.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 23,
        "name": "Squaring the Circle III",
        "description": "MENU: “We haven’t gotten answers yet, but we’ve made a little progress. \nMENU: “More information helps. More context helps.”\nMENU: “Even if we don’t find something with a direct connection to the labs, I feel like we’re on the right track.”\nMENU: “Next, visit the Blooming Tree and make scavenging rolls.”\nMENU: “The weather here is always clear. It wasn’t lightning, so what blasted that tree apart?\nMENU: “It probably won’t open any doors for us, but I’m still curious.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 24,
        "name": "Squaring the Circle IV",
        "description": "MENU: “Visit the Airplane Crash and scavenge around with your Kami.”\nMENU: “I haven’t mentioned that plane until now, but that’s because I have no clue where it came from or what it’s doing here.\nMENU: “I’m supposed to have pretty thorough data for this area!”\nMENU: “It’s not a gap I feel an absence from like the starter town or the labs data, this thing is a genuine foreign body.”\nMENU: “What’s the story? Who was on it? Where did they go? Could we follow them?”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 25,
        "name": "Squaring the Circle V",
        "description": "MENU: “Visit the Clearing and do a little scavenging. Do your best to not disturb the cairn.”\nMENU: “Mounds of stone like this are often meant as burial mounds.\nMENU: “So who or what is buried here?”\nMENU: “With every dead end we lose another lead and pile on more junk data.”\nMENU: “Let’s hope this one has something useful.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 26,
        "name": "Squaring the Circle VI",
        "description": "MENU: “Let’s keep working our way around the perimeter of the map. Go back to the Labs Entrance one more time and make scavenging rolls.”\nMENU: “Where did that building come from and why is it sealed up so well? Who sealed it up like that?”\nMENU: “It honestly really bothers me. When we get the doors open, I’m going to have so many questions.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 27,
        "name": "A Forgotten Friend",
        "description": "MENU: “Let’s cut the boundary pushing. I remembered something.”\nMENU: “Go to the Lost Skeleton and make scavenging rolls. Let’s give the place a thorough check.”\nMENU: “That skeleton has a business laptop. That’s definitely an employee from the labs!”\nMENU: “Something’s been making me overlook him until now, but I won’t miss anything this time.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 28,
        "name": "Deeper Understanding",
        "description": "MENU: “Try the Scrap Confluence for something that might be able to read a data chip.”\nMENU: “There’s so much tech there, some of it is bound to work.”\nMENU: “Fingers crossed you find a laptop battery.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 29,
        "name": "Computer Blues",
        "description": "MENU: “Try the Marketplace room for anything that might be able to read a data chip.”\nMENU: “That’s the only working computer around here, I think.”\nMENU: “Just go buy something and look for an SD card port while you’re doing it.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 30,
        "name": "Humility",
        "description": "MENU: “I’ve been avoiding this for a while, but I think we should go ask Mina for help.”\nMENU: “Mina is kind of scary. She’s also completely foreign to my databases, like that crashed jet, but Mina is alive.”\nMENU: “And independent. And powerful!”\nMENU: “She’s been giving you quests. I can read them too, you know.”\nMENU: “That means she can take control over parts of my interface… It’s not nice.”\nMENU: “On the other hand, this also makes it more likely that she can help us.”\nMENU: “What would be a nice welcoming gift for someone like that? Flowers?”\nMENU: “No, I’ve got the perfect idea. When you visit on my behalf, just fold a big stack of $MUSU in the greeting card.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 31,
        "name": "Pyramid Power",
        "description": "MENU: “With that item from Mina, you should be able to power up that laptop.”\nMENU: ”So go do it! Fire that baby up!”\nMENU: ”I want to see what’s on that chip!”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 32,
        "name": "Safe Hex",
        "description": "MINA: “That was a mean prank on my part, but I knew you could handle it.”\nMINA: ”Water can be an effective barrier for spirits.”\nMINA: ”I thought, strange thing that you are, that you might make it. Alas, no luck.”\nMINA: ”Lucky for you, as a goddess of all that flows, I can help out with the waterfall.”\nMINA: “This kind of thing might stay beyond your reach for a while, but I can simply do it for you.”\nMINA: ”Collect the proper reagents for me and I will cast a charm that will let you walk under flowing water.”\nMINA: ”It’ll practically last forever.”\nMINA: ”We’ll start with something that has a sticky and water-resistant nature.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 33,
        "name": "Holier Than Thou",
        "description": "MINA: “Next, some Holy Syrup.”\nMINA: “The holy syrup will help form a barrier against the purifying effects of flowing water.”\nMINA: “It also makes the potion spread more smoothly.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "account": {
          "accepted": false,
          "complete": false,
          "requirementsMet": false
        }
      },
      {
